                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Highly recommended for puzzle fans and those with a logical mind.  \n\nMove the blocks around so that all the colored ones touch, each color to it's own.  I used the mouse to click and drag the blocks.  There are 9 worlds or sections or whatever you want to call them, and in each one they introduce a new concept that makes the game harder, such as blocks that are linked and move together or sticky blocks.  \n\nFor completionists there are 2 more facets of the game other than just solving the puzzle.  1. Find all the white orbs that are hidden behind the blocks.  There is one orb in each level.  2. After you solve the puzzle try to get the blocks so that they cover the weird symbols to get illumination.  That's where it gets tough.  There are multiple ways to solve some of the levels.\n\nThe graphics are nice and colorful.\n\nThe music is whimsical but does not intrude on the game.  It's really nice background music for a puzzle game.  I like it a lot.\n\nI've got over 7 hours so far and have just started the 7th world.\n\nUPDATE:  Finished all the levels in all 9 worlds.  Now trying for all illumination--very difficult.  Some seem impossible.  But after getting all of the moon pearls (the white orbs hidden in every level) it revealed a secret 10th world!  This game is awesome.  One of the best puzzle games I've ever played.\n\nUPDATE #2:  They added more puzzles, but they are easier than the other ones.  I think they were the ones in Blockwick 1 on mobile app.  Also, the price has increased since I bought the game.",
